[{:db/id -1
  :adr/id "adr-2809081300-consistency-manifest-field-shape"
  :adr/title "Where :consistency attaches in the logic manifest -- per-effect (format v2) vs module-level default :local (widens ADR-2809052250)"
  :adr/status "proposed"
  :adr/date "2026-09-08"
  :adr/related ["ADR-2809052250" "ADR-2607279200" "ADR-2809051130"]
  :adr/context
  "ADR-2809052250 established the four-class vocabulary {:local :validated :countersigned :inga-qc} and its world-CID binding rules, but deliberately left open where the value attaches in the compiler manifest. This document decides that shape. Surveyed amu origin/main 42d303f6779 (worktree kototama-consistency-7-cons): src/kotoba/compiler/logic_manifest.cljc builds kotoba.logic-manifest/v1 with required-input-keys #{:definition-cid :artifact-cid :compiler-contract :semantics-cid :world-cid :dependency-cids :intent-schema-cids :resource-bounds} plus computed rows :kir-sha256 :effects :wire-effects :function-effects :manifest-sha256. :effects is the flat module-level semantic set (semantic-effects of the KIR effect set); :function-effects is a vector of {:name :effects :wire-effects} giving per-function granularity that already exists today. :consistency is not a field. build! is library-only (referenced by README + test_runner + biscuit interop), not wired into amu compile CLI emission, and lang/code-identity.edn records :package-manifest-cid :status :not-implemented -- so whatever shape is chosen here has no landing surface in compile output yet. Per ADR-2607279200 language-surface changes land only with a passing compile; therefore this ADR fixes the shape as design and leaves emission blocked until :package-manifest-cid exists."
  :adr/decision
  "1. Attach :consistency per-effect, not as a module-level scalar -- because a module may legally mix effects of different evidence classes (a :local read next to a :inga-qc order), a single module-level :local default would erase that distinction and make the stronger claims unrepresentable at the module boundary. 2. Concretely, extend the existing :function-effects rows so each {:name :effects :wire-effects} gains the consistency class per semantic effect; the flat module-level :effects stays the fail-closed union (:local for any effect whose class is not statically decided). This reuses the per-function seam that already exists, so no new top-level authorization key is introduced and authorizer projection (amu:requires over :effects) keeps its current arity. 3. This is a format change: the manifest shape changes, so :format advances (kotoba.logic-manifest/v1 -> v2) and, because the manifest is content-addressed, the definition CID of the manifest schema changes -- recorded as definition-CID churn, not as a bug. 4. Fail-closed default per ADR-2809052250 decision 2: any effect whose consistency class cannot be resolved against world CIDs attaches :local. No effect ever promotes itself (no-implicit-consistency-promotion, landed in surface-status.edn via PR kotoba-lang#625 commit 121c509). 5. Emission stays blocked: no amu compile output carries :consistency until :package-manifest-cid is implemented and a compile run actually admits AND rejects on the vocabulary (per ADR-2607279200). This ADR only fixes the shape."
  :adr/consequences
  "Fixes the open shape question from ADR-2809052250 so downstream work (capability-semantics :consistency-classes entry, peer re-execution, task-4 fork evidence) can target a concrete manifest shape. Cost: the v1 manifest format is not backward-compatible for consumers that read :function-effects, but there are no production consumers today (build! is library-only), so the format bump is free. Does NOT land any compiler change; emission remains gated on :package-manifest-cid and a passing compile. Next concrete step after this ADR lands as accepted: add a :consistency-classes map to lang/capability-semantics.edn :logic and a format-v2 fixture to amu logic_manifest tests, both gated on passing compiles."}]
